The points $A(1,2)$, $B(5,4)$ and $C(3,8)$ are given. Use the dot product to show that $\angle ABC=90^{\circ}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (A) at (1,2);
\coordinate (B) at (5,4);
\coordinate (C) at (3,8);
\draw[black] (A)--(B)--(C)--cycle;
\path (A) node[below left] {$A$};
\path (B) node[right] {$B$};
\path (C) node[above] {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
